import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
---

<InfoLayout title="Editorial Process | FreeOnlineToolkit" description="Learn about the editorial process behind FreeOnlineToolkit.org — how we research, verify, and maintain our free online calculators and tools.">
  <h1 class="animate-in">Editorial Process</h1>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1"><em>Last updated: May 2026</em></p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-compass"></i> Our Editorial Philosophy</h2>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">At FreeOnlineToolkit.org, we believe that free online tools should be accompanied by clear, accurate, and helpful editorial content. Every calculator on our site exists within an editorial framework that includes a unique overview, methodology explanation, real-world example, and tool-specific FAQs. Our goal is not just to give you a number — but to help you understand what the number means and how to use it.</p>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i> Research and Methodology</h2>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Each tool on our platform begins with thorough research into the underlying formulas, standards, and data sources. Our process includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1"><strong>Formula identification:</strong> We identify the standard formula or methodology used by professionals in the field — whether that's the amortization formula used by banks, the Mifflin-St Jeor equation used by dietitians, or the Naegele rule used by obstetricians.</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-2"><strong>Source verification:</strong> Formulas and data are verified against authoritative sources including government agencies (IRS, CDC, CFPB, USPTO), peer-reviewed research, and industry standards bodies.</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-3"><strong>Reference documentation:</strong> Whenever possible, we cite authoritative sources on the tool page so you can verify the methodology yourself and explore further reading.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-flask"></i> Testing and Quality Assurance</h2>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Before any tool is published, it undergoes systematic testing:</p>
  <ul>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1"><strong>Known-input testing:</strong> Each calculator is tested with known inputs and the output is compared against verified results from authoritative sources or manual calculation</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-2"><strong>Edge case handling:</strong> Zero values, negative inputs, very large numbers, and boundary conditions are tested to ensure graceful handling</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-3"><strong>Cross-browser testing:</strong> Tools are tested on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge to ensure consistent behavior</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-4"><strong>Mobile responsiveness:</strong> All tools are tested on mobile devices and tablet screen sizes</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i> Content Creation</h2>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">Each tool page includes unique editorial content created specifically for that tool:</p>
  <ul>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1"><strong>Tool overview:</strong> A unique introductory paragraph explaining the purpose and relevance of the tool</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-2"><strong>Methodology explanation:</strong> A clear explanation of how the calculation works and the formula behind it</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-3"><strong>Real-world example:</strong> A concrete example with actual numbers showing the calculation step by step</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-4"><strong>Tool-specific FAQs:</strong> Frequently asked questions written specifically for that tool, addressing common user concerns</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-5"><strong>References:</strong> Links to authoritative sources for further reading and verification</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-rotate"></i> Content Updates and Maintenance</h2>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">We maintain our content on an ongoing basis through:</p>
  <ul>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1"><strong>Regular reviews:</strong> Tool pages are reviewed periodically. Each page displays a "last updated" date indicating the most recent editorial review.</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-2"><strong>Formula updates:</strong> When tax brackets, interest rates, medical guidelines, or other reference data change, we update the relevant calculators and content.</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-3"><strong>User feedback:</strong> We review all user submissions and address reported issues promptly. If an error is found, it is corrected and the page date is updated.</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-4"><strong>New additions:</strong> We regularly add new tools based on user requests and emerging needs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-solid fa-link"></i> Sources and References</h2>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">We rely on authoritative sources for our formulas and data, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1"><strong>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)</strong> — BMI guidelines, growth charts, health statistics</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-2"><strong>World Health Organization (WHO)</strong> — BMI classification standards, global health data</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-3"><strong>Internal Revenue Service (IRS)</strong> — Tax brackets, standard deductions, retirement contribution limits</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-4"><strong>Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB)</strong> — Mortgage guidelines, consumer financial protection</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-5"><strong>Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS)</strong> — CPI inflation data, employment statistics</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-6"><strong>U.S. Patent and Trademark Office (USPTO)</strong> — Patent fee schedules, filing procedures</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-7"><strong>National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST)</strong> — Unit conversion standards, measurement guidelines</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-8"><strong>U.S. Department of Energy (DOE)</strong> — Fuel economy data, solar energy guidelines</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-9"><strong>American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG)</strong> — Due date calculation, fertility guidelines</li>
    <li class="animate-in animate-in-delay-10"><strong>Peer-reviewed research</strong> — Published studies for formulas such as Mifflin-St Jeor (resting energy expenditure), US Navy method (body fat estimation), and Devine/Robinson/Miller/Hamwi (ideal weight calculations)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="animate-in"><i class="fa-regular fa-envelope"></i> Contact Our Editorial Team</h2>
  <p class="animate-in animate-in-delay-1">If you have questions about our editorial process, find an error in one of our tools, or have a suggestion for improvement, we welcome your feedback. Visit our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> to get in touch with the editorial team.</p>
</InfoLayout>
